Description: elanmoc: read the matched user_id with finger-info on 0c77
 The ELAN:ARM-M4 0c77 (FW 0x312) does not implement get-userid
 (43 21 <slot>): the command is never answered, on either the command
 endpoint (0x83) or the MoC endpoint (0x84), so every read runs into the
 5s ELAN_MOC_CMD_TIMEOUT. That breaks two paths - elanmoc_list(), which
 fprintd runs after every failed match to reconcile its storage, and the
 lookup after a successful match.
 .
 The FW implements finger-info (40 ff 12 <slot>) instead, which carries
 the same user_id payload one byte further into the frame behind a 0x40
 header, and answers immediately for empty slots with a zero length.
 Verified against the chip with depau/elanpoc: slot 0 returns
 'FP1-20260629-7-3B6325D6-alessandro', slots 1-9 return length 0, and the
 command still answers when issued directly after a match.
 .
 Using it keeps the upstream logic intact, in particular the check that
 the finger the chip matched is actually the one in the gallery: reporting
 a match without that check would authenticate any finger enrolled on the
 chip - including another user's - as the first print of the gallery.
